  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) of Indonesia is currently overseeing the verification process for vice presidential candidates. A dedicated verification team has coordinated with multiple state institutions, including the Supreme Court, the National Police, and the Ministry of Finance, to validate candidate documentation and health examination results. While the Minister of Home Affairs confirmed that civil registry documents for the candidates align with verification findings, the assembly has provided a four-day window for candidates to rectify any remaining administrative shortcomings. Simultaneously, internal parliamentary debates have emerged regarding the selection procedure for a successor to Gibran Rakabuming Raka. Some political factions advocate for a consensus-based approach, while other legislators maintain that the process should adhere strictly to constitutional provisions, including potential voting procedures in a plenary session.",
